# fixedbugs, M-c-callbacks step 0, 2026-09-05 (panel 111 R4).
#
# SYMPTOM: a callback declared with the wrong signature stopped the compiler
# with `assert failed: !found.is_err()` and no file, no line and no code — the
# worst shape a compiler failure has, because there is nothing in it for the
# author to act on. `atexit` wants `void (*)(void)`; this case declares the
# handler as taking an `i64`.
#
# CAUSE: when clang refuses a probe, `emit/ffi.hero` REBUILDS the probe line to
# work out which parameter the column belongs to — and it built its name table
# with `ctype.new_names` alone, which holds no typedef for a function type. So
# `ctype.func_of`'s assertion fired, correctly: it refuses to guess a name. The
# gap was latent before the permission, because every other boundary type spells
# itself without a table, and it is the same class of defect as the probe's own
# second spelling table — one question, two answers, one of them not grown.
#
# FIX: `explain` builds its table with `ctype.with_functions`, which is the
# table the emitter wrote the line with. Rebuilding a text with a different
# table would have mis-numbered the columns even where it did not assert.
#
# WHAT IT PRODUCES NOW, and it also scores a panel prediction as FALSIFIED: the
# ffi-pragmatist seat predicted a callback mismatch would reach exit 2 because
# no reader classifies an argument-position function-pointer mismatch. Measured:
# clang's text contains ` to parameter of `, which is the needle panel 071's
# MISMATCHED family already reads, so it was exit 1 on this line before any code
# was minted for it. The class below is `ffi_callback_type` all the same, opened
# by author decision 2026-09-05 over the coordinator's recommendation: the two
# mistakes want the same repair sentence and DIFFERENT SEARCHES, and a reader
# chasing a callback should not have to sift every width mismatch in the
# language. The note was wrong too, and it is chosen by the type now (§4.17).

extern "stdlib.h"
    function atexit(f: (function(i64) -> ())) -> i32  #~ ffi_callback_type

function bye(_: i64)
    print("bye")

function main()
    if atexit(bye) != 0
        print("atexit refused the handler")
